WEBVTT

00:03.730 --> 00:05.530
A dinner invitation?

00:05.970 --> 00:06.830
But why?

00:07.070 --> 00:07.400
Count Hyde Baronial Residence

00:07.400 --> 00:11.170
Count Hyde Baronial Residence
I'm inviting you
and Captain Abriel.

00:11.170 --> 00:11.370
I'm inviting you
and Captain Abriel.

00:11.370 --> 00:13.340
The tiniest noble's
mansion in all of the empire.
Don't you get it?

00:13.340 --> 00:16.670
The tiniest noble's
mansion in all of the empire.
Does this have anything to do
with the death of your brother?

00:17.510 --> 00:18.310
Yes.

00:18.510 --> 00:22.450
Tomorrow would've been my
brother's birthday if he were alive.

00:23.080 --> 00:25.720
Obviously he can't be there
to celebrate with us.

00:25.720 --> 00:29.090
I want to have a party with people
who had a connection with him.

00:29.520 --> 00:30.730
Well...

00:30.730 --> 00:34.530
...we might have had a connection,
but maybe not the right kind.

00:34.530 --> 00:35.560
I mean...

00:35.560 --> 00:38.500
I understand your concerns...

00:38.500 --> 00:40.140
...but what's past is past.

00:40.140 --> 00:42.470
The only people who knew
my brother in this star system...

00:42.470 --> 00:44.500
...are you two and me.

00:45.240 --> 00:48.080
You're not suggesting I celebrate
his birthday all by myself?

00:48.080 --> 00:50.110
I wasn't saying that, but...

00:50.110 --> 00:50.780
All right.

00:50.780 --> 00:53.250
Now, I've got a favor to ask you.

00:54.580 --> 00:56.820
I want you to extend
this invitation...

00:56.820 --> 00:59.050
...to Captain Abriel...

00:59.050 --> 01:02.050
...or rather, to Viscountess Paryunu,
on my behalf.

01:02.590 --> 01:07.730
I realize that it's my duty
to personally invite her...

01:07.730 --> 01:09.330
...but, you know...

01:09.330 --> 01:11.600
...this is a rather personal issue...
- Which means that...

01:11.600 --> 01:14.240
...if Lafiel refuses this invitation...

01:14.240 --> 01:16.200
...I can avoid going as well.

01:16.200 --> 01:17.010
I'm sure you can...

01:17.010 --> 01:19.110
I understand. I will go and...

01:19.110 --> 01:20.480
Oh, right.

01:20.480 --> 01:24.100
Even if the Princess refuses,
you'll still come, right?

01:24.450 --> 01:25.210
What?!

01:25.410 --> 01:28.150
I'd hate to have to
cancel my reservation.

01:28.150 --> 01:29.170
That would be embarrassing.

01:30.590 --> 01:31.950
Of course!

01:33.620 --> 01:37.490
Make sure you tell her that
this is a personal invitation.

01:37.490 --> 01:39.520
Okay! I'll be counting on you!

01:41.160 --> 01:43.470
When I thought about it...

01:43.470 --> 01:45.900
...I had never met her brother
Klowal, the Baron Febdash.

01:46.770 --> 01:49.370
But by the time I realized that...

01:49.370 --> 01:51.530
...the transmission was over.

01:57.680 --> 02:01.450
Remembrance Dinner

02:07.290 --> 02:11.950
Banner of the Stars

03:27.440 --> 03:29.700
Commander Atosuryua
said that?

03:29.700 --> 03:32.140
I was thinking of turning it down.

03:32.140 --> 03:33.040
Why turn it down?

03:33.510 --> 03:34.030
What?

03:34.810 --> 03:36.210
I'm going.

03:36.210 --> 03:38.050
You will be coming, too,
won't you?

03:38.050 --> 03:41.280
But it's to celebrate
the baron's birthday!

03:41.280 --> 03:43.270
You mean the late baron.

03:43.820 --> 03:45.550
Uh, right...

03:49.390 --> 03:50.790
In any case...

03:50.790 --> 03:53.630
...why would you want to
celebrate the birthday...

03:53.630 --> 03:55.190
...of someone you killed?

03:56.400 --> 03:59.390
To alleviate your guilt?

04:01.600 --> 04:02.930
What is it then?

04:04.510 --> 04:07.380
Celebrating the birthday of
someone who has died...

04:07.380 --> 04:09.040
...can have a special significance.

04:09.510 --> 04:10.530
Like a funeral?

04:11.250 --> 04:12.510
Not quite.

04:13.110 --> 04:17.020
What happens if no one
remembers you after you die?

04:17.350 --> 04:20.760
Wouldn't it be sad if
no one was upset that...

04:20.760 --> 04:21.810
...you'd passed away?

04:22.320 --> 04:23.380
It's depressing.

04:24.160 --> 04:24.990
I guess so.

04:25.660 --> 04:27.630
So, while we're still alive...

04:27.630 --> 04:29.630
...I think it's good to take time...

04:29.630 --> 04:31.430
...to remember those who died.

04:31.430 --> 04:33.770
That way, maybe when
it's our turn to go...

04:33.770 --> 04:36.900
...someone might return the favor
and remember us.

04:36.900 --> 04:38.700
I guess so.

04:39.270 --> 04:40.070
Well...

04:41.040 --> 04:42.410
...in my case...

04:42.410 --> 04:44.280
...even years after I die...

04:44.280 --> 04:47.910
...I don't think there's anyone
who's going to miss me.

04:57.930 --> 05:00.720
Look after the ship while I'm gone.

05:01.360 --> 05:03.300
I'll be back as soon as possible.

05:03.300 --> 05:03.970
Yes.

05:03.970 --> 05:06.400
If anything comes up,
I'll contact you.

05:10.100 --> 05:11.370
Are you there?

05:11.370 --> 05:12.570
Diaho?!

05:13.310 --> 05:15.800
He doesn't seem to want to
leave my side.

05:17.480 --> 05:19.250
Even if I were gone...

05:19.250 --> 05:21.220
...I doubt he'd even miss me.

05:22.120 --> 05:24.850
So, I'll leave him with you.

05:24.850 --> 05:26.790
If anything should happen to him...

05:26.790 --> 05:28.760
I'll get a hold of you?

05:28.760 --> 05:30.820
You may handle the situation.

05:32.390 --> 05:33.450
I'll leave it to you.

05:34.100 --> 05:37.430
We'll take care of Diaho,
so you go enjoy yourselves!

05:37.630 --> 05:40.330
I can't say I'm looking
forward to this.

05:44.370 --> 05:45.770
Let's get going...

05:45.770 --> 05:47.540
...Supply Officer Lin.

05:47.540 --> 05:48.740
Right.

05:48.740 --> 05:50.040
Everything's ready over here.

05:50.040 --> 05:52.170
Releasing the Calike.

05:59.050 --> 06:02.520
I didn't know there were
fancy restaurants in Dakul.

06:02.520 --> 06:03.860
Of course there are.

06:03.860 --> 06:07.920
Didn't you have places
like that on your home planet?

06:09.630 --> 06:11.760
Well, I was little,
so I don't remember much...

06:12.070 --> 06:16.130
...but I doubt we had anything like
the ones you have here in space.

06:17.040 --> 06:18.170
In any case...

06:18.170 --> 06:20.480
...whatever we might have
had in space...

06:20.480 --> 06:22.710
...for Landers like us...

06:22.710 --> 06:24.870
...we would've always
gotten homesick.

06:25.250 --> 06:26.610
Is that right?

06:27.080 --> 06:28.880
What about you?

06:28.880 --> 06:31.750
I mean, remember the time
we landed in Sufugnoff?

06:31.750 --> 06:33.690
You felt homesick for space,
right?

06:35.920 --> 06:37.860
Yes, I did.

06:38.390 --> 06:39.560
But that was...

06:39.560 --> 06:41.830
...because everything
was so ridiculous.

06:41.830 --> 06:44.060
You can't compare the two.

06:47.140 --> 06:48.540
What's so funny?

06:48.540 --> 06:50.940
By ridiculous, do you mean
your disguise?

06:50.940 --> 06:52.240
Everything was ridiculous.

06:52.770 --> 06:54.710
The destruction of the Gosroth...

06:54.710 --> 06:57.080
...being stopped by
Baron Febdash...

06:57.280 --> 07:00.750
...and the fact that our arrival
at Sufugnoff was delayed...

07:00.750 --> 07:03.110
...and our allies were attacked
as a result.

07:03.280 --> 07:05.620
And the emergency landing
on the surface of the planet.

07:06.020 --> 07:07.010
Yeah.

07:07.560 --> 07:08.990
I guess it was ridiculous.

07:10.790 --> 07:12.130
Out of the whole thing...

07:12.130 --> 07:14.400
...you forcing me to dye my
hair black...

07:14.400 --> 07:15.930
...is something I'll never forget.

07:15.930 --> 07:18.170
We didn't have a choice.

07:18.170 --> 07:20.870
Otherwise, we would've been caught.

07:20.870 --> 07:23.400
I'm not criticizing you.

07:23.400 --> 07:26.270
Or was it actually meant
as an insult?

07:26.470 --> 07:27.670
Of course not.

07:32.150 --> 07:33.810
You're right.

07:34.050 --> 07:36.520
I wanted to get back to space.

07:41.720 --> 07:43.990
Lafiel, is everything okay?

07:44.330 --> 07:45.660
Don't make me out to be a fool.

07:45.830 --> 07:47.260
Of course I'm okay!

07:56.970 --> 07:58.440
But you know...

07:58.440 --> 08:01.380
...I was pretty scared myself
back then.

08:01.380 --> 08:04.280
I don't know if I'd have
made it on my own.

08:05.510 --> 08:06.880
What about you?

08:07.650 --> 08:08.380
Jinto...

08:08.380 --> 08:09.440
Huh?

08:09.750 --> 08:11.580
I think we've almost arrived.

08:16.560 --> 08:18.460
Welcome to Mitsugoiwa.

08:18.460 --> 08:20.360
Please identify yourselves.

08:20.800 --> 08:23.920
This is First Princess Abriel
Nei Dubrusk Paryunu Lafiel.

08:24.400 --> 08:27.730
This is Count Jinto
Lin Syune Rock Hyde.

08:28.200 --> 08:30.900
We were invited by
Unit Commander Atosuryua.

08:32.010 --> 08:33.370
That has been confirmed.

08:33.370 --> 08:35.000
Please proceed to number 16.

08:43.580 --> 08:45.110
This is impressive!

08:45.320 --> 08:48.420
There's even a separate
dock for Calikes!

08:48.420 --> 08:49.760
When needed...

08:49.760 --> 08:53.020
...it allows the heads of planetary
nations to eat together here.

09:14.950 --> 09:16.850
People are opening doors...

09:16.850 --> 09:19.220
This must be a pretty
high-class restaurant.

09:20.450 --> 09:23.590
The commander shares the
same tastes as her late brother.

09:23.590 --> 09:24.180
Yeah.

09:43.010 --> 09:46.570
Actually, the commander has
much better taste than the baron.

09:48.420 --> 09:50.750
Uh, yeah. I think so.

09:56.860 --> 09:58.330
Her Highness the First Princess...

09:58.330 --> 10:01.660
...and His Excellency
Count Hyde have arrived.

10:05.370 --> 10:08.940
It was good of you to come here
in honor of my late brother.

10:08.940 --> 10:11.230
I would like to thank you
on his behalf.

10:11.470 --> 10:13.570
Your Highness. Your Excellency.

10:13.710 --> 10:16.640
The pleasure is ours, Baroness.

10:16.640 --> 10:17.800
Yes, thank you.

10:22.850 --> 10:23.620
Well...

10:23.620 --> 10:26.520
...I want us all to feel
relaxed and comfortable.

10:26.720 --> 10:29.850
Let's set aside our ranks
in the Star Forces.

10:30.020 --> 10:34.430
And I'll try my best to set aside
your place in royalty.

10:35.100 --> 10:37.030
I've taken the liberty of ordering.

10:37.030 --> 10:38.620
I hope you don't mind.

10:40.940 --> 10:42.000
Well, then...

10:42.000 --> 10:43.130
...to my brother!

10:52.210 --> 10:57.210
My brother's body is still heading
toward the center of the galaxy.

10:59.990 --> 11:01.590
Even if we had retrieved it...

11:01.590 --> 11:03.760
...we'd have sent it into space anyway...

11:03.760 --> 11:05.780
...so there's really no difference.

11:08.500 --> 11:09.160
However...

11:09.160 --> 11:11.000
...when we read my brother's will...

11:11.000 --> 11:14.900
...it said that he wanted his body
sent outward from the galaxy.

11:14.900 --> 11:15.570
Oh, well.

11:15.570 --> 11:18.440
I guess he won't mind,
since he is dead, after all.

11:18.640 --> 11:20.660
I'm very sorry to hear that.

11:21.140 --> 11:23.240
It's all right, Your Highness.

11:23.240 --> 11:26.210
My brother chose the path
he wanted to take.

11:26.210 --> 11:27.150
Besides...

11:27.150 --> 11:30.450
...that ship of his was quite nice.
Called 'The Lady of Febdash'.

11:30.450 --> 11:33.420
I don't think we could have
found a more expensive coffin!

11:35.060 --> 11:38.230
Although I never did like
the name of that ship.

11:38.230 --> 11:41.300
At first I thought he'd
named it after me...

11:41.300 --> 11:43.360
...but he told me he didn't.

11:43.360 --> 11:46.430
Who else could he have
named it after?

11:46.430 --> 11:47.700
Who knows?

11:47.900 --> 11:50.100
Maybe it was a secret lover.

11:50.100 --> 11:53.970
But I don't think he was the type
to name his ship after a lover.

11:54.180 --> 11:56.910
Maybe he was convinced that...

11:56.910 --> 11:58.910
...the only thing a true Abh
can love...

11:58.910 --> 12:01.180
...was the love of flying itself.

12:02.580 --> 12:04.780
My poor brother.

12:04.990 --> 12:08.940
The pressure to conform
as an Abh was getting to him.

12:09.590 --> 12:10.320
I see.

12:12.360 --> 12:14.930
When you think about it, it's
an odd combination.

12:14.930 --> 12:16.120
It's a bit like...

12:16.600 --> 12:19.260
Please don't mind me.

12:19.500 --> 12:21.100
I'm a Lander by birth...

12:21.100 --> 12:24.240
...and was only given the
status of an Abh later.

12:24.240 --> 12:28.110
Your father was from the
same noble family as me.

12:28.110 --> 12:31.700
As his genetically altered offspring,
you are a first generation Abh.

12:32.280 --> 12:33.650
And the captain...

12:33.650 --> 12:37.950
...and her clan have been part of the
Abh nobility from the beginning.

12:38.220 --> 12:42.260
It's like the three of us are a model
of the evolutionary process.

12:42.260 --> 12:44.730
That's not true, Jinto.

12:44.730 --> 12:46.630
We did not evolve.

12:47.030 --> 12:49.100
We were merely adapted...

12:49.100 --> 12:50.720
...as the Kin of the Stars.

12:51.500 --> 12:52.630
That's right.

12:52.830 --> 12:56.130
We can't evolve using
artificial methods.

12:56.600 --> 12:59.610
People can't create anything
more than what they are.

12:59.610 --> 13:01.440
Compared to our ancestors...

13:01.440 --> 13:03.880
...we simply have an
extra sensory organ...

13:03.880 --> 13:05.350
...and we live longer.

13:06.050 --> 13:07.110
Even so...

13:07.110 --> 13:09.710
...that's quite an achievement.

13:29.940 --> 13:31.700
This is...

13:33.210 --> 13:34.240
What's the matter?

13:34.240 --> 13:36.780
I'm sorry if I chose
something you don't like.

13:36.780 --> 13:38.940
No, it's not that.

13:39.380 --> 13:40.810
It's just that this is...

13:41.880 --> 13:45.720
...what the baron served when
I dined with him at Febdash.

13:45.720 --> 13:48.220
Oh, is that right?

13:48.220 --> 13:52.630
Actually, I tried to reproduce the
same menu my brother served you.

13:53.190 --> 13:55.530
We found a record of it, so...

13:57.100 --> 13:58.870
Is there something else?

13:58.870 --> 14:00.730
No. Nothing at all.

14:01.070 --> 14:03.000
I was just a little taken aback.

14:06.870 --> 14:10.370
I had to leave your brother's
dinner before we'd finished.

14:11.510 --> 14:13.310
I didn't know about that part.

14:13.510 --> 14:14.280
Well then...

14:14.480 --> 14:18.690
...I hope you'll keep me company
until the end of the meal tonight.

14:18.690 --> 14:20.820
The circumstances
aren't the same...

14:20.820 --> 14:22.620
...but at least the menu is!

14:23.390 --> 14:25.090
I thought it might be fun to...

14:25.090 --> 14:27.860
...get a sense of how he entertained
the Princess and the Count.

14:27.860 --> 14:30.460
Actually, I wasn't there.

14:30.460 --> 14:33.570
I was with the previous baron
then.

14:33.570 --> 14:34.690
In other words...

14:35.600 --> 14:39.330
...I was having dinner with
your father, Commander.

14:40.710 --> 14:43.040
I didn't know that either.

14:43.640 --> 14:46.380
In other words, the invitation
was extended...

14:46.380 --> 14:48.510
...only to the Princess?

14:49.780 --> 14:52.780
That's exactly the sort
of thing he'd do.

14:53.290 --> 14:54.660
Baroness...

14:54.660 --> 14:56.750
...I want you to be honest.

14:56.960 --> 14:59.050
Are you sure you don't hate me?

14:59.860 --> 15:01.360
Your Highness...

15:01.360 --> 15:03.330
Despite our short history...

15:03.330 --> 15:04.990
...we are a proud family.

15:05.230 --> 15:08.470
How can our descendants
preserve such pride...

15:08.470 --> 15:12.100
...knowing I've invited you to
dinner only to insult you?

15:12.570 --> 15:13.970
You're right.

15:13.970 --> 15:15.480
Forgive me.

15:15.480 --> 15:17.000
It was a silly question to ask.

15:18.110 --> 15:19.700
My brother and I...

15:20.550 --> 15:22.850
I do have some wonderful
memories about him.

15:23.050 --> 15:26.250
But most of them date back
to our childhood.

15:26.950 --> 15:28.990
Once we grew up, we drifted apart.

15:28.990 --> 15:31.620
And we didn't see
each other very much.

15:38.030 --> 15:40.330
This was one of my
brother's favorites.

15:40.330 --> 15:44.670
But your brother didn't seem
to have much of an appetite.

15:44.870 --> 15:45.600
Really?

15:45.810 --> 15:47.210
He was probably just nervous.

15:47.810 --> 15:50.910
He'd lose his appetite
when he was nervous.

15:50.910 --> 15:52.450
Thanks to that...

15:52.450 --> 15:54.050
...you could tell something was up.

15:54.050 --> 15:56.220
He just wouldn't touch his food!

15:56.220 --> 15:57.210
I see.

15:57.820 --> 15:58.920
So...

15:58.920 --> 16:01.650
...what sort of food
did your brother like?

16:03.560 --> 16:05.390
Let's see...

16:05.390 --> 16:09.290
As a child I remember he really
liked pears boiled in syrup.

16:09.900 --> 16:14.630
I was amazed at how he could
eat something so sickly sweet.

16:15.000 --> 16:18.200
I'm sure his tastes changed
when he grew up.

16:18.970 --> 16:22.200
The food here is a bit sweet,
so he'd probably love it.

16:25.010 --> 16:27.450
One thing my brother liked
was dogs.

16:27.450 --> 16:28.140
What?!

16:28.620 --> 16:29.710
As pets.

16:30.920 --> 16:33.020
For one with such
a complicated past...

16:33.020 --> 16:35.850
...you still seem to have your
cultural biases.

16:36.020 --> 16:38.460
But he had a cat.

16:38.460 --> 16:42.920
He firmly believed that cats were
more suitable pets for an Abh.

16:43.660 --> 16:45.130
Ever owned a cat?

16:45.130 --> 16:46.430
Count?

16:47.130 --> 16:49.660
Yes, I have. It is
the Princess's nephew.

16:51.040 --> 16:52.970
You sure are persistent.

16:52.970 --> 16:54.140
Well, well...

16:54.140 --> 16:57.440
Seems like some kind of
inside joke.

16:57.440 --> 16:58.580
From that moment...

16:58.580 --> 17:01.010
...the commander took over.

17:01.380 --> 17:04.610
She spent the evening sharing
memories of her brother.

17:04.890 --> 17:08.720
Lafiel became more comfortable
as she listened carefully.

17:08.720 --> 17:11.430
I then realized that this was...

17:11.430 --> 17:14.490
...a sort of memorial to help
her close a chapter.

17:42.160 --> 17:44.430
All ships have now passed
through the Aptic Gate!

17:44.430 --> 17:46.690
All ships report their condition!

17:46.690 --> 17:50.100
The operation to defend the
Aptic System has now begun!

17:50.100 --> 17:51.600
Ships seeking to re-supply...

17:51.600 --> 17:53.230
...must follow the orders
of local supply officers.

17:53.230 --> 17:55.130
So, we have twelve fleets.

17:56.070 --> 17:57.810
This is perfect, Nereis.

17:57.810 --> 17:58.930
Take a look.

18:00.070 --> 18:02.080
If we had more than twelve fleets...

18:02.080 --> 18:03.780
...we would run out of supplies...

18:03.780 --> 18:05.540
...and our range would be limited.

18:06.210 --> 18:07.410
Besides...

18:07.410 --> 18:10.210
...we don't have room to deploy
a bigger fleet here anyway.

18:11.020 --> 18:14.420
That's only if we hole up
in the Sord, right?

18:14.420 --> 18:16.520
Isn't that what you intended?

18:16.520 --> 18:18.590
That's exactly what I intended.

18:18.590 --> 18:21.760
But one should never presume
such things, Nefee.

18:22.030 --> 18:25.560
Then why don't we confront
the enemy in Plane Space?

18:26.130 --> 18:30.400
We're going to have to go up
against at least 150 enemy fleets.

18:30.400 --> 18:33.340
We can't expect much reinforcement
to help us hold them at bay.

18:34.740 --> 18:36.070
I know that.

18:36.280 --> 18:37.340
If that's the case...

18:37.340 --> 18:39.470
I said I know that, Nefee.

18:40.650 --> 18:43.480
I know you well,
so it doesn't bother me much...

18:43.480 --> 18:45.780
...but you should change
your attitude.

18:46.020 --> 18:49.010
I'm not like this with anyone
but you, brother.

18:49.320 --> 18:51.260
I suppose I should feel honored.

18:51.460 --> 18:52.220
Probably.

18:53.990 --> 18:55.160
Look.

18:55.160 --> 18:56.960
That's our battlefield.

19:00.470 --> 19:02.660
So, it's going to be a
regular space battle.

19:03.340 --> 19:05.570
It's not very edifying...

19:05.570 --> 19:09.670
...considering we have the power
to roam around in Plane Space.

19:09.980 --> 19:11.240
What are you hinting at?

19:11.810 --> 19:13.800
This is a battle in regular space.

19:14.450 --> 19:17.780
We can show them what we
learned in Star Forces training.

19:19.150 --> 19:21.760
A battle in regular space
at such a scale...

19:21.760 --> 19:23.950
Don't you think it's artistic?

19:24.860 --> 19:26.990
It's most important that
we win, right?

19:26.990 --> 19:28.790
That's what you said.

19:29.730 --> 19:32.400
What can you say if it turns into
a form of art?

19:32.400 --> 19:33.270
But...

19:33.270 --> 19:36.170
...I won't make it my
sole objective, dear brother!

19:36.740 --> 19:40.200
As you know, I am the one
with common sense.

19:40.970 --> 19:43.580
If you're the one with
such common sense...

19:43.580 --> 19:46.880
...then I don't want to have
anything to do with it...

19:46.880 --> 19:47.740
...Nefee.

19:54.760 --> 19:58.210
It looks like Admiral Bebaus
has arrived.

19:58.760 --> 20:01.430
You think this is going to be
the main battleground?

20:01.430 --> 20:03.190
Sounds like you don't want to fight.

20:04.830 --> 20:08.490
I think I was more nervous
about going to that dinner.

20:09.200 --> 20:10.800
I'm only now feeling relieved.

20:11.610 --> 20:15.040
And you seemed to be having an
awkward time of it, too.

20:15.040 --> 20:16.940
It's not my forte.

20:16.940 --> 20:18.410
Mourning the dead.

20:18.410 --> 20:20.880
The only time I ever talked
to the Baron...

20:20.880 --> 20:23.580
...was when I talked to him
over the radio.

20:23.780 --> 20:25.840
Not even a conversation.

20:26.390 --> 20:30.090
It's not like I had a friendly
conversation with him either.

20:30.090 --> 20:31.920
Still, we did our duty.

20:32.130 --> 20:33.790
To mourn his death.

20:33.790 --> 20:34.820
"Our duty," huh?

20:37.830 --> 20:39.870
I think I'd rather be forgotten...

20:39.870 --> 20:42.230
...than have someone
mourn me out of duty.

20:42.900 --> 20:44.710
It's not a duty for the dead.

20:44.710 --> 20:46.370
It's a duty for those left behind.

20:48.580 --> 20:49.540
I see.

20:49.540 --> 20:52.570
How was your dinner party,
Captain?

20:56.580 --> 20:58.050
Don't leer at me like that!

20:58.950 --> 20:59.990
Anything happen while we were away?

20:59.990 --> 21:00.820
No.

21:00.820 --> 21:02.320
Nothing in particular.

21:02.320 --> 21:04.690
The food was pretty average.

21:06.930 --> 21:08.130
Um...

21:08.130 --> 21:11.360
Which do you prefer, Samson,
cat or dog?

21:13.170 --> 21:15.100
Well, I like them both...

21:15.100 --> 21:17.270
...but if I had to choose...

21:17.270 --> 21:18.840
...I'd go for cats.

21:18.840 --> 21:20.510
Is that...

21:20.510 --> 21:23.570
...a hint of your strange
eating customs?

21:25.080 --> 21:26.840
Just a tiny one.

21:27.480 --> 21:28.950
Don't worry.

21:28.950 --> 21:32.790
I'm not so starved that I'd eat
a friend's pet for dinner.

21:32.790 --> 21:33.820
However...

21:33.820 --> 21:35.790
...don't bring him
to the bridge so much.

21:35.790 --> 21:39.120
There's a lot of sensitive
equipment there.

21:39.390 --> 21:41.530
If the hairs from your kitty cat...

21:41.530 --> 21:44.530
...cause some kind of malfunction...

21:44.530 --> 21:48.070
...I might get a sudden urge
to eat some rutimond...

21:48.070 --> 21:49.230
Rutimond?

21:50.570 --> 21:54.400
It's a delicacy made by boiling
the meat of a certain animal.

21:55.710 --> 21:58.840
I haven't tasted it in twenty years.

22:00.310 --> 22:02.820
What popped in my mind then...

22:02.820 --> 22:07.150
...was not the pathetic sight of
Diaho being boiled up by Samson...

22:08.390 --> 22:10.860
A friend's pet... Friend's...

22:11.290 --> 22:12.220
A friend...

22:13.360 --> 22:16.850
It's not like I had a friendly
conversation with him either.

22:17.460 --> 22:19.070
Still, we did our duty.

22:19.070 --> 22:20.870
To mourn his death.

22:20.870 --> 22:22.300
"Our duty," huh?

22:22.300 --> 22:24.400
I think I'd rather be forgotten...

22:24.400 --> 22:26.700
...than have someone
mourn me out of duty.

22:26.940 --> 22:28.940
It's not a duty for the dead.

22:28.940 --> 22:30.770
It's a duty for those left behind.

22:31.580 --> 22:33.210
Regardless...

22:33.210 --> 22:36.550
...I'll already be dead when
people are mourning for me.

22:37.220 --> 22:39.150
I don't care how I'm remembered.

22:39.920 --> 22:45.460
Besides, I have no family or
friends left to mourn for me.

22:45.460 --> 22:48.290
I don't even have a place
I can truly call home.

22:49.700 --> 22:51.760
That's what I thought.

22:54.300 --> 22:58.600
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.140 --> 23:03.410
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.750 --> 23:08.340
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.750 --> 23:13.380
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.520 --> 23:15.760
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.760 --> 23:19.620
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:21.030 --> 23:26.170
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:26.170 --> 23:29.730
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.070 --> 23:34.130
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.670 --> 23:39.210
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.210 --> 23:46.390
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.390 --> 23:51.530
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.530 --> 24:00.090
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.070 --> 24:07.210
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.210 --> 24:12.380
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.380 --> 24:20.980
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.420 --> 24:25.690
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.470 --> 24:32.700
In a place like this?!

24:32.700 --> 24:33.670
Shooting!

24:35.800 --> 24:36.390
Enemy attack?!

24:37.100 --> 24:38.370
Is it a direct hit?!

24:38.370 --> 24:40.410
Space-time fusion!

24:40.410 --> 24:41.510
Enemy assault ship...

24:41.510 --> 24:42.740
...targeting on us!

24:42.740 --> 24:45.150
Focus magnetic shield
on the right hull!

24:45.150 --> 24:47.210
Use the anti-proton cannon
to shoot them down!

24:47.210 --> 24:49.380
The ship will respond
in ten seconds!

24:49.380 --> 24:50.880
Eight... seven...

24:50.880 --> 24:52.320
- We're not going to make it!
...six...

24:52.320 --> 24:55.020
...five... four... three...

24:55.290 --> 24:57.860
We've become stranded
in Plane Space!

24:57.860 --> 25:00.850
Next Episode...
Escape in the Dark
